text:
Reviewed the whole repo. Existing tests pass (`6 passed`), and bytecode compilation passes when pycache is redirected out of the read-only workspace. I would **not approve this as-is**.

Overall score: **5/10**. The code is small and readable, but the ingestion path is not production-safe: it can leave stale rows, partially commit failed ingests, crash on malformed-but-plausible input, and silently accept invalid identifiers. Estimated significant rewrite/change: **180 lines**, mostly in `evalmerge/pipeline.py` plus tests.

